00:50:14.220 --> 00:50:16.900
- Mm-hmm, so

00:50:18.353 --> 00:50:21.420
I think there's this one idea

00:50:21.420 --> 00:50:22.630
that I really like

00:50:23.760 --> 00:50:25.480
that I think it was

00:50:27.990 --> 00:50:29.730
Professor Mitch Resnick who built,

00:50:29.730 --> 00:50:33.090
there's this software
for children to, Scratch,

00:50:33.090 --> 00:50:34.713
to learn programming,

00:50:35.580 --> 00:50:39.420
this like visual way of
how children can program

00:50:39.420 --> 00:50:43.080
